{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>They shall be set in gold in their fullness.</b> That is, the stones shall be in their fullness set in gold, and Scripture commands that the stones be upon the gold and the letters upon the stones, and they were seventy-two letters corresponding to seventy-two names." "<b>And there is</b> here a great awakening toward the preciousness of the Torah, for it is more precious than pearls and all desirous things cannot compare with it (Proverbs 3:15). For since silver and gold are the desire of human beings, and precious stones are above gold, therefore Scripture comes to rouse us that the Torah surpasses all acquisitions altogether — for see, gold is the base for the precious stones, and the stones are the base for the letters. And so it is the way to make a base from the lesser for the weightier; and if so, the letters are the essence of all, for through them the world was created, since all acquisitions are found in it."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:05:06.813570567Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}